  "analysis": "I'm starting fresh in /app. The task is to reverse-engineer a programmatically-rendered image at image.ppm and write a C program (image.c) that regenerates a near-identical image to reconstructed.ppm, achieving >=0.8 normalized L2 similarity. I must NOT read image.ppm in the program itself, but I can analyze it now to figure out what algorithm generated it.",
  "plan": "First, explore the environment: check for image.ppm, its size, and the PPM header (format, dimensions, max value). Then dump some pixel data to understand the rendering. I'll use the file command, head, and a quick Python/xxd analysis if available.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "file image.ppm\n",
